{
  "about": "Shopping results in a reply (#682, ADR 113): a ```products fence holds a JSON list (or one product), the first is the pick. Read the same on the web page (Products.parse in public/products.js, test/products-web.test.js) and in the Android app. `products` is what a fence holds once read, or null when it stays a code block; `off` is how much less than `was` in whole percent, and `was` is kept only with it. `amounts` are prices and their numbers (null: none). `drafts` are replies still being written and what is drawn of them: a products fence waits whole until it is closed. A rule changes here and in both apps together.",
